[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-94448"] :question/problem "Let $f(x,y)={x}^{2}-4y,$ where $x=2st$ and $y={s}^{2}t.$ Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂s}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069068/assets/21cec766fe72965697304ef4288ffb2b090ddfca179210165dbcfd42ec490b27.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t)$ and $y=y(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2x,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =2(2st)=4st, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂s} & =2t, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂s} & =2st.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂s} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s} \\\\  & =(4st)(2t)+(-4)(2st) \\\\  & =8s{t}^{2}-8st \\\\  & =8st(t-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-94747"] :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069068/assets/21cec766fe72965697304ef4288ffb2b090ddfca179210165dbcfd42ec490b27.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t)$ and $y=y(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =-\\frac{1}{({e}^{st})^{2}}=-{e}^{-2st}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =-\\frac{1}{({e}^{-st})^{2}}=-{e}^{2st}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂s} & =t{e}^{st}, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂s} & =-t{e}^{-st}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂s} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s} \\\\  & =(-{e}^{-2st})(t{e}^{st})+(-{e}^{2st})(-t{e}^{-st}) \\\\  & =t{e}^{st}-t{e}^{-st} \\\\  & =t({e}^{st}-{e}^{-st}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-94813/selection/e999c4abe5fa27798bbb76b7f2342c8f66406a24a0e729cfb62ecb0481181cab" :answer/id #uuid "d245bd8d-566f-561b-a623-f8d7a5be3694" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2t{e}^{2s+{t}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94813/selection/100e747ace793d199b0e9bd4eda3c9e053de3946dab45f9f0827c03a75add4c2" :answer/id #uuid "4091250c-7695-5baf-ba82-311a7d20076d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "st{e}^{2s+{t}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94813/selection/29ee62bdce7fb7640807865cad91da67e5bf22fe01d34ab8177dd83cc6fd661b" :answer/id #uuid "2b89daae-b256-5c93-87cc-b28b654fad98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(t+2){e}^{2s+{t}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94813/selection/65f83ec7c6e3c85e9842d38781dc65ff9b8668c211ec584578929baee2e3db63" :answer/id #uuid "303ef2df-4798-5c6e-a1da-3514b057cdd2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({t}^{2}-1){e}^{2s+{t}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94813/selection/5fad4671f263b48ca76358075e01574c7a1943dd5a8407cb2d456dcff78a214c" :answer/id #uuid "08658397-2af8-577b-be9d-b0c1d27357d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{t}^{2}{e}^{2s+{t}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94813/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "73434767-a57d-5756-8581-c4b42bcddadf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94813/selection/e999c4abe5fa27798bbb76b7f2342c8f66406a24a0e729cfb62ecb0481181cab" :answer-field/choices ["q-94813/selection/e999c4abe5fa27798bbb76b7f2342c8f66406a24a0e729cfb62ecb0481181cab" "q-94813/selection/100e747ace793d199b0e9bd4eda3c9e053de3946dab45f9f0827c03a75add4c2" "q-94813/selection/29ee62bdce7fb7640807865cad91da67e5bf22fe01d34ab8177dd83cc6fd661b" "q-94813/selection/65f83ec7c6e3c85e9842d38781dc65ff9b8668c211ec584578929baee2e3db63" "q-94813/selection/5fad4671f263b48ca76358075e01574c7a1943dd5a8407cb2d456dcff78a214c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94813" :question/id #uuid "0a6b18b5-6eca-5bcb-8bc4-42eedbe5cf58" :question/math-academy-id "q-94813" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)={e}^{x+y+z},$ where $x=s-t,$ $y={t}^{2}$ and $z=s+t.$ Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂t}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069068/assets/b593a1b60fe8c1aef2c5c229ff426db350e6296b9ecb767494283f0fa3342072.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y,z)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t),y=y(s,t)$ and $z=z(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x,y$ and $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={e}^{x+y+z},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={e}^{x+y+z},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}={e}^{x+y+z}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & ={e}^{(s-t)+{t}^{2}+(s+t)}={e}^{2s+{t}^{2}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & ={e}^{(s-t)+{t}^{2}+(s+t)}={e}^{2s+{t}^{2}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & ={e}^{(s-t)+{t}^{2}+(s+t)}={e}^{2s+{t}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂t} & =-1, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂t} & =2t, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂t} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂t} & =({e}^{2s+{t}^{2}})\\cdot (-1)+({e}^{2s+{t}^{2}})\\cdot 2t+({e}^{2s+{t}^{2}})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-{e}^{2s+{t}^{2}}+2t{e}^{2s+{t}^{2}}+{e}^{2s+{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =2t{e}^{2s+{t}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-94813/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "71c243ca-5d46-58d2-bd16-28075c04d2db"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94813"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-94814"] :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069068/assets/be6afcdd0ad9ae0d7ef377c4918442a64e1186c90c25e27ec6c224d816a602fd.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y,z)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t),y=y(s,t)$ and $z=z(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x,y$ and $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=4,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=3,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂s} & =4s, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂s} & =1, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂s} & =8s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂s} & =(4)\\cdot 4s+(3)\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot 8s \\\\  & =16s+3-16s \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-95114/selection/11b2ebb4b23f93bb52f2790a10cbd87e0af11cec536c6b87cfa966a01d5d1691" :answer/id #uuid "67ca6dfb-d6af-559c-82bf-ebef070247b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1+3{x}^{4}}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95114/selection/a606395d0e0747f871453863e67c3ca006116a5b9d1ae7ca33d5586cb8219253" :answer/id #uuid "b5a3ad7f-7674-54d8-8241-16b0a9d49b0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95114/selection/21dcf71faaf85c84472fa2360ac7847943abe10866d82757af9b2f6cbc8a8ffc" :answer/id #uuid "2e7e3d5f-ce3f-53a2-8ca5-49d857f63430" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{4}}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95114/selection/f00790495c696cf9136bac81b18fa9af9539069f0f26803b91dcf5b4a566e6f5" :answer/id #uuid "440cc302-7062-5eb8-8252-a123c74e21eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1+{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95114/selection/e83ff372fd780710678cc2deedc9d3de4549964ed6dde8d9fe2bc4e86bf46de8" :answer/id #uuid "9360bdf0-1ac6-5f4f-8bb4-9a6cd43a5b95" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1+3{x}^{3}}{x\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95114/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6e425e93-f692-5345-8f23-5bdc03925a49" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-95114/selection/11b2ebb4b23f93bb52f2790a10cbd87e0af11cec536c6b87cfa966a01d5d1691" :answer-field/choices ["q-95114/selection/11b2ebb4b23f93bb52f2790a10cbd87e0af11cec536c6b87cfa966a01d5d1691" "q-95114/selection/a606395d0e0747f871453863e67c3ca006116a5b9d1ae7ca33d5586cb8219253" "q-95114/selection/21dcf71faaf85c84472fa2360ac7847943abe10866d82757af9b2f6cbc8a8ffc" "q-95114/selection/f00790495c696cf9136bac81b18fa9af9539069f0f26803b91dcf5b4a566e6f5" "q-95114/selection/e83ff372fd780710678cc2deedc9d3de4549964ed6dde8d9fe2bc4e86bf46de8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-95114" :question/id #uuid "da628d4c-a325-5343-bcd6-7344b3c8f181" :question/math-academy-id "q-95114" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}$ and $y={x}^{3},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{x}^{6}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}(1+{x}^{4})}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{x\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{x}^{6}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}(1+{x}^{4})}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{x\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}\\cdot 3{x}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}+\\frac{3{x}^{4}}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+3{x}^{4}}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-95114/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1457941c-efa8-556f-9df7-3c5ae7b44ced"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-95114"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
